    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## Problem\nOccasionally got this error after 15008855.\n```\nError in LspNotify Autocommands for \"<buffer=1>\":\nLua callback: runtime/lua/vim/lsp/semantic_tokens.lua:779: attempt to index local 'state' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        runtime/lua/vim/lsp/semantic_tokens.lua:779: in function 'reset_timer'\n        runtime/lua/vim/lsp/semantic_tokens.lua:293: in function 'send_request'\n        runtime/lua/vim/lsp/semantic_tokens.lua:223: in function <runtime/lua/vim/lsp/semantic_tokens.lua:214>\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec_autocmds'\n        runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:864: in function <runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:862>\n```\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nnvim --clean --cmd \"lua vim.lsp.config('a', { cmd = { 'emmylua_ls' }, filetypes = { 'lua' }}) vim.lsp.enable('a')\" \\\n                            --cmd \"lua vim.defer_fn(function() vim.lsp.enable('a', false) vim.lsp.enable('a', true) end, 1000)\" a.lua --headless\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\nNo error.\n\n\n## System info\n\n- Nvim version (nvim -v): `v0.13.0-dev-836 gf3fbb3928c` neovim/neovim@f3fbb3928c\n- Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?: ?\n- Operating system/version: Linux 7.0.13-zen1-1-zen\n- Terminal name/version: kitty\n- $TERM environment variable: `xterm-kitty`\n- Installation: ?\n\n",
